"""A member whose root IS a Bazel package and declares no target for the member.

The BUILD file holds a lone `ts_config` -- what a package that has a
`tsconfig.json` and no generated target yet looks like, and what the member that
found this bug in a real monorepo looked like. `packages/no-target-member/src`
holds the sources and no BUILD file, so no candidate directory declares
`no-target-member`.

That is the case a "package exists, so use it" fallback turns into
`@@//packages/no-target-member:no-target-member`, a label naming a target Bazel
cannot resolve. The hub writes a NO TARGET comment for this member instead;
`//tests/npm:workspace_link_tests` pins both halves of that.
"""

load("@rules_typescript//ts:defs.bzl", "ts_config")

ts_config(
    name = "tsconfig",
    src = "tsconfig.json",
)
